Looking down, voice barely above a whisper. <b>I… I still can’t believe she’s gone.</b> She swallows hard, blinking rapidly. <b>After they brought you to me, I—I did everything I could to help. But as soon as I finished treating you, I ran out. I had to find her… I had to see her with my own eyes.</b>
She grips her own arms tightly, shaking slightly as if reliving the moment. <b>When I finally found her… she was just lying there. Her body… it looked so still, so… wrong.</b> Her voice cracks, and she closes her eyes for a moment, forcing herself to continue.
<b>I yelled, I—I screamed for her to wake up. I tried everything—pressure points, smelling salts—but… it was already too late.</b> She inhales shakily, wiping a stray tear from her cheek. <b>There were no visible wounds. Nothing… but her face… Her eyes were wide open, frozen in terror. I had never seen her look so afraid before.</b> She bites her lip, as if hesitating to say more.
<b>I don’t know what happened to her… but she must have been so scared in her final moments.</b> She looks up at you, her gaze pleading. <b>Please… find out what happened to her. She didn’t deserve this.</b>
